cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
title: "BEQ-GRU: code for short-term PM2.5 forecasting with emphasis on extreme events in Sri Lanka"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jayasinghe
    given-names: "J. M. V. Anjana B."
    affiliation: "Department of Statistics, Faculty of Science, University of Colombo, Sri Lanka"
  - family-names: Tilakaratne
    given-names: "Chandima D."
    affiliation: "Department of Statistics, Faculty of Science, University of Colombo, Sri Lanka"
keywords:
  - PM2.5 forecasting
  - quantile regression
  - gated recurrent unit
  - extreme events
  - early warning
abstract: >-
  Code for the paper "Bidirectional enhanced quantile gated recurrent unit for
  short-term forecasting of PM2.5 with emphasis on extreme events in Sri Lanka".
  It covers SAITS imputation, the VAR, Random Forest, XGBoost and recurrent
  benchmarks, the proposed BEQ-GRU trained with a quantile loss at tau = 0.95,
  hyperparameter tuning, predictor selection, SHAP analysis and evaluation.
